Based on this survey, what is the probability that Jo is elected President, with either Britt or Louis as Vice-President?

solutions.latex:
Let $F$, $I$, $J$ be the people who chose French, Italian and Japanese. Work from the centre outwards, starting with $n(F\cap I\cap J)=4$:
$$\begin{aligned}F\cap I\cap J&:\ 4\\ F\cap I\text{ only}&:\ 11-4=7\\ F\cap J\text{ only}&:\ 10-4=6\\ I\cap J\text{ only}&:\ 7-4=3\\ F\text{ only}&:\ 26-7-6-4=9\\ I\text{ only}&:\ 22-7-3-4=8\\ J\text{ only}&:\ 18-6-3-4=5\\ \text{none of the three}&:\ 45-(9+7+8+6+4+3+5)=3\end{aligned}$$
\exfigure{402_q27_s1}

